   "unmapped": [
    "P processors select a batch of P actions per round; rewards of the whole batch revealed only at the end of the round (fixed batch size P, regret summed over T*P queries)",
    "reward function f* is eps-close in sup-norm to a function class F with bounded eluder dimension; learner knows eps",
    "function values bounded by a known constant B (|f(x)| <= B for all f in F)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "we consider the (parallel) contextual linear bandit setting where at each round $t$, the $p$-th bandit learner receives a context $\\cX_{t,p} \\subset \\mathbb{R}^d$ and a master algorithm $\\cA$ commands each learner to select an action $\\x_{t, p} \\in \\cX_{t,p}$ ... $r_{t, p} = \\fstar(\\x_{t,p}) + \\xi_{t, p}$ ... minimize the parallel regret $\\cR(T, P) = \\sum_{p=1}^{P} ( \\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\fstar(\\x_{t, p}^\\star) - \\fstar(\\x_{t, p}) )$"
  },
